<p>Israel established a clandestine military outpost in the Iraqi desert to support its air campaign against Iran, The Wall Street Journal reported, citing people familiar with the matter, including U.S. officials. The facility was built shortly before the U.S.-Israeli campaign against Iran began on Feb. 28 and housed Israeli special forces, served as a logistics hub for the Israeli Air Force and included search-and-rescue teams for any downed Israeli pilots, according to accounts citing the Journal. The report said Israeli forces launched airstrikes on Iraqi troops who nearly discovered the site in early March after a shepherd reported unusual military activity, including helicopter movements, in a remote area. Iraqi authorities said at the time that one Iraqi soldier was killed and two others were wounded, condemned the operation as unauthorized, and later complained to the United Nations about foreign forces carrying out strikes on Iraqi territory, initially attributing the attack to the United States. The Journal cited a person familiar with the matter who said the United States did not take part in that attack; Reuters said it could not independently verify the Journal report, and Israel&#x27;s military declined comment to JNS while the Israeli prime minister&#x27;s office did not immediately respond to Reuters.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Consent gap: Several accounts said U.S. officials knew of the facility but Iraq had not approved it.</li></ul><blockquote>It appears there was a certain force on the ground before the strike, supported from the air, operating beyond the capabilities of our units - Lt. Gen. Qais al-Muhammadawi</blockquote><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639817-israel-secret-iraq-base/'>Israel built secret base in Iraq to bomb Iran – WSJ</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/israel-built-and-defended-a-secret-base-in-iraq-for-iran-war-report-11473187#publisher=newsstand'>Israel Built And Defe